  "passage": {
    "title": "A Weekend in Edinburgh",
    "paragraphs": [
      {
        "label": "A",
        "text": "Edinburgh is the capital of Scotland. It is a beautiful city with a famous castle on a hill in the middle. Every year, more than four million tourists visit it, and many of them come in August for the big arts festival."
      },
      {
        "label": "B",
        "text": "My friend Clara and I went there last June for a weekend. We took the train from London, and the journey was four and a half hours. We stayed in a small hostel near the station. It was cheap, only twenty-five pounds a night, but the beds were not very comfortable."
      },
      {
        "label": "C",
        "text": "On Saturday, we walked up to the castle. The tickets were nineteen pounds each, which seemed expensive, but the view of the city was amazing. In the afternoon, we visited a museum about Scottish history. It was free, so we stayed for two hours. In the evening, we had dinner in a pub and listened to live music."
      },
      {
        "label": "D",
        "text": "On Sunday morning, it rained, so we did not climb the hill called Arthur's Seat as we planned. Instead, we went shopping on Princes Street and bought presents for our families. Our train home left at six o'clock. We were tired, but we both agreed that it was a great weekend, and we want to go back in August for the festival."
      }
    ]
  },
